# An anchor is a position-scoped binding, so redefining one is a state
# transition rather than a mistake, and an alias binds to whichever state is
# in force where the alias is written. This is one document: anchors do not
# cross a `---`, so a sequence of states lives inside one.
--- !node &Rollout
first: &state
  port: 80
early_reader: *state
second: &state
  port: 443
late_reader: *state
